 put salt in our  wounds the iPad Pro in 2015 with a  lightning Port ran at USB 3.0 speeds  compared to a 2022 almost 2023 phone  that actually needs the better transfer  with those large files and apple still  did not do that even with the a16 so  that means that if they do give us USB  type c it can still be the same super  slow USB 2.0 and that would be  incredibly frustrating now why would  they do that well there are a few  reasons when I looked into you how to  transfer these large files and to do the  conversions and what Apple wants to do  with it they blatantly advertise you to  just use airdrop to send files to your  Mac or to just upgrade your iCloud  storage so you can store these super  large files with the link directly to do  that that is why Apple limited this port  which in 2015 ran 10 times faster to  still have that super slow speed and I  don't think that would change next year  because for Apple they make money with  you buying their iCloud storage and with  you using airdrop because that means you  have to have a Mac which is why I am  stuck in the ecosystem because it is  very convenient so because of that I  think it's very naive to think that the  USB type-c port will give us fast data  transfers and I don't want a USB type-c  port that is limited now some people  want it because they want to have faster  charging and I would like that but once  again with this iPad even though it has  a USB type-c port the charging speed is  actually limited compared to the iPad  Air even though there's no reason to do  that they have the same batteries inside  there but Apple did limit that I want  something that is going to be an actual  Improvement instead of what we have now  which is severely limited including Max  save charging and I'll explain why now  that we're talking about wireless  charging this Halo lock mini kickstand  Wireless power bank from our sponsor ESR  has really impressed me because compared  to the Apple Mac say power bank it was  able to give me a lot more charge and  the charge is faster than anchors while  having the strongest magnets it has that  kickstand which apples doesn't and the  charging port is on the side so you can  use it as a desk charging station and  the battery pack doesn't stick below the  6.1 inch iPhones like the anchor does  also unlike apples you can turn off  wireless charging if you you don't want  it to charge which is great when you're  using it as a stand with that ESR it's  really great reviews and it's actually  quite a bit less expensive compared to  the other options we also have a 10 000  milliamp hour model if you're trying to  get the highest capacity so check out  the link in the description to pick up  one of these ESR haloc wireless chargers  for a killer price and start wireless  charging today now personally I have  been wireless charging my iPhone almost  exclusively ever since magsafe came out  with the iPhone 12. I am a huge fan of  magsafe it is so convenient I've made  many videos covering the top accessories  including comparisons with different  Wireless power Banks but some people say  well you still have to have a data  connection but you guys may be wrong  that could all change very soon now  there are two things that really  frustrate me about macsafe and one is  the fact that Apple locks out third  parties from having that 15 in what  capability but with that even though the  max 8 Puck is rated at 15 watts that  doesn't last long after that first  initial burst it actually drops down to  6 Watts which is lower than what ESR  offers on theirs or other companies  offer so they're not maximizing it and  other companies they're not allowed to  do that unless you're paying apple and  you're limiting it to what they want  personally I want faster charging  similar to what OnePlus has done where  they have 50 watt Chargers that charge  way faster than lightning does with the  iPhone more than what Apple allow you  with USB type c now we don't need 