at you actually need to have a  physical connection for example recovery  of your phone or if you want to back it  up then things like that now most people  nowadays only use the lightning to  charge everything's done through iCloud  and that's what Apple would prefer and  of course they make more money that way  with iCloud backup now if you think  that's weird to use that for data that  might be slow well this port is  incredibly slow the iPad 10 sport is  incredibly slow and if you think about  it fiber optic cable for gigabit it is  insanely fast and there was a study done  showing that wireless fiber optic light  transfer reaches 42 gigabit per second  that is like about 90 times faster than  this lightning port and that is actually  faster than Thunderbolt 4 data transfer  it is absolutely insane so not only is  Apple hold a patent to this it works  incredibly well and they could easily do  that now personally I would also really  like a focus on faster airdrop airdrop  is great but it's actually not that fast  if you're transferring photos as that's  what I found when I was trying to send  these huge raw files from my iPhone to  my computer and with that what gives me  proof that Apple doesn't want to add USB  type-c to their iPhone and they'd rather  bypass the eu's regulations is the fact  that their brand new airpods Pro 2  instead of switching to USB type c like  they have on other devices even on beat  stuff they did on this iPad they are  sticking with a lightning connector and  these things usually only get updated  every three years they are still doing  this and that just shows me that they  would rather just stick it to the EU use  another method that you can license and  make more money on and we know they've  wanted a portless iPhone they like  making money and they like having  control and not having other people tell  them what to do so you guys let me know  your thoughts are you excited about usb  type-c coming does the speeds matter or  Apple'